  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-16",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "○島原藩"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "島原藩（しまばらはん）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "The maru-marker opening Shimabara domain's entry — the only marker on this page. Everything to its RIGHT is read earlier and closes the preceding domain, 新發田藩; everything to its LEFT is Shimabara's. Shimabara is the Matsudaira (Fukōzu) domain on the Hizen peninsula, best known as the seat of the 1637-38 Shimabara Rebellion."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "○島原藩"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1245,1376,107,559"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-17",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "肥前高來郡 豐後宇佐郡 豐後國東郡"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "肥前高来郡（ひぜんたかくぐん）・豊後宇佐郡（ぶんごうさぐん）・豊後国東郡（ぶんごくにさきぐん）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "The districts holding Shimabara's lands, printed as a warichu under the marker: Takaku district in Hizen (the Shimabara peninsula itself), plus Usa and Kunisaki districts across the strait in Bungo. Read the RIGHT sub-run first (肥前高來郡), then the LEFT (豐後宇佐郡), then the second right-hand run (豐後國東郡). The scattered Bungo holdings are a reminder that a domain's kokudaka often aggregated non-contiguous parcels."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "島原藩領郡名"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1240,1942,126,748"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-18",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "高 七萬四千八百七十貳石三斗壹升壹合壹勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "高（たか） 七万四千八百七十二石三斗一升一合一勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Assessed kokudaka: 74,872.3111 koku. Place value pivots on 萬 and reads right to left: 7×10,000 + 4×1,000 + 8×100 + 7×10 + 2. The sub-koku units run strictly descending — 石 > 斗 (.1) > 升 (.01) > 合 (.001) > 勺 (.0001) — and terminate at 勺. Note the formal numerals (貳, 壹) used for the fiscal figure, against the plain 二 of the military counts on the same page."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "高（島原藩分）"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1122,1042,87,1604"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-19",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "本高井新田畑改出高共"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "本高並びに新田・畑改出高共（ほんだかならびにしんでん・はたかいでだかとも）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Warichu note qualifying the 高 above: 'base high together with the new-paddy and dry-field reclamation increases.' Read the RIGHT sub-run first (本高井新田), then the LEFT (畑改出高共). The 井 is the standard Edo/Meiji abbreviation for 幷/並 ('and, together with') — verified at 10x as a true 井 (continuous verticals through both crossbars, no detached 丷). The note matters analytically: the 74,872 koku is a combined working figure, not the bare formal rating."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "(原朱) 本高井新田畑改出高共（島原藩分）"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:1112,2733,118,340"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-20",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "正税 現米三萬六千九百四十五石七斗四升壹合六勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "正税（せいぜい） 現米三万六千九百四十五石七斗四升一合六勺"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Regular land tax, stated in 現米 ('actual rice', the rice actually delivered rather than a nominal assessment): 36,945.7416 koku — about 49 percent of the 74,872.3111 koku high in the column to the right. Sub-units descend 石 > 七斗 (.7) > 四升 (.04) > 壹合 (.001) > 六勺 (.0006), terminating at 勺. NOTE: MASTER labels this row 正租; the page prints 正税 (禾 + 兌, with the 丷 top and the outward-hooking 儿 leg), not 租 (禾 + 且). Verified at 9x against reference renderings of both glyphs — trusting the scan."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "正税（島原藩分）"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/lower_p083_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
        "type": "FragmentSelector",
        "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/",
        "value": "xywh=pixel:986,1051,91,1929"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "anno-shibata_lower_p083_left-21",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "藩制一覽表第七（島原）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "藩制一覧表 第七（島原）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Running header (柱) in the outer margin: 'Table of Domain Institutions, Fascicle 7 — (Shimabara)'. 覽 is the kyūjitai of 覧. This is PROVENANCE, not data: it names Shimabara because Shimabara's entry begins on this page, even though ten of the fourteen data columns belong to 新發田藩. 第七 is a fascicle number, not a data theme."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "page header（藩制一覧表）（島原藩分）"
      }
